# Implementation Plan: Brain Consolidation Feature

> **Version:** v0.4.0 (Nucleus MCP Feature)  
> **Date:** 2026-01-06  
> **Status:** 🟡 Awaiting Approval

---

## Goal

Implement Brain Consolidation as a **Nucleus MCP feature set**, enabling any editor (Antigravity, Cursor, Windsurf, Claude Desktop) to manage brain artifact hygiene.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This plan proposes adding 4 MCP tools and 4 CLI commands to Nucleus. The Phase 1 tool ([brain_archive_resolved](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#2058-2072)) runs automatically in [nightly_agent.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/scripts/nightly_agent.py). Phases 2-4 are on-demand.

---

## Feature Hierarchy (4 Tiers)

| Tier | Name | Automation | Risk | Reversible? |
|:-----|:-----|:-----------|:-----|:------------|
| **1** | Archive Resolved | Automated (nightly) | ✅ Zero | Yes (move) |
| **2** | Propose Merges | On-demand (CEO) | 🟡 Low | Yes (proposals only) |
| **3** | Execute Merges | Human-triggered | 🟡 Low | Yes (originals archived) |
| **4** | Prune Archive | Manual only | 🔴 High | ❌ No (true delete) |

---

## Proposed Changes

### Nucleus MCP Server

#### [MODIFY] [__init__.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py)

Add 4 new core logic functions and 4 MCP tool wrappers:

**Core Functions:**
```python
# Tier 1: Archive
def _archive_resolved_files() -> dict:
    """Move *.resolved.* files to archive/resolved/"""
    
# Tier 2: Propose (Future)
def _propose_merges() -> list:
    """Detect redundant docs and suggest merges"""

# Tier 3: Execute (Future)
def _execute_merge(proposal_id: str) -> dict:
    """Execute an approved merge, archive originals"""

# Tier 4: Prune (Future - Deferred)
def _prune_archive(days: int, confirm: bool) -> dict:
    """Delete files older than N days (requires confirm=True)"""
```

**MCP Tools:**
- [brain_archive_resolved()](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#2058-2072) - Tier 1 (implement now)
- `brain_propose_merges()` - Tier 2 (stub for future)
- `brain_execute_merge()` - Tier 3 (stub for future)
- `brain_prune_archive()` - Tier 4 (stub for future, requires manual confirm)

---

#### [MODIFY] [cli.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/cli.py)

Add [consolidate](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/cli.py#844-916) subparser with commands:

```bash
nucleus consolidate archive   # Tier 1: Archive resolved files now
nucleus consolidate propose   # Tier 2: Show merge proposals
nucleus consolidate execute   # Tier 3: Execute approved merges
nucleus consolidate prune     # Tier 4: Prune old archive (requires --confirm)
```

---

### Nightly Agent Integration

#### [MODIFY] [nightly_agent.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/scripts/nightly_agent.py)

Add call to [_archive_resolved_files()](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#1747-1826) in the nightly routine:

```python
def run_brain_consolidation():
    """Tier 1: Automated nightly cleanup"""
    # Import from nucleus or call via CLI
    result = subprocess.run(["nucleus", "consolidate", "archive"], capture_output=True)
    if result.returncode == 0:
        emit_event("brain_consolidated", "ROUTINE", {"output": result.stdout.decode()})
```

---

## Hierarchy vs. Structuring (Clarification)

| Concern | Part of Consolidation? | Notes |
|:--------|:----------------------|:------|
| **Moving [.resolved](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/.gemini/antigravity/brain/7c654df4-b83e-43f9-8620-f15868ec39d1/task.md.resolved) files** | ✅ Yes (Tier 1) | This plan |
| **Merging redundant docs** | ✅ Yes (Tier 2-3) | Future |
| **Creating folder hierarchy** | ❌ No (Structuring) | Different feature |
| **Renaming files** | ❌ No (Structuring) | Different feature |
| **Cross-linking docs** | ❌ No (Knowledge Graph) | Different feature |

**Structuring** (folder hierarchy, naming conventions) is a **separate feature** that we can spec out later. Consolidation is specifically about **reducing redundancy and noise**.

